swer odd or even? Try 3 + 5 and 7 + 9 before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Odd and even", "p": ["Even numbers end in 0, 2, 4, 6 or 8."], "qq": {"id": "m4u03s3t01", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Is 37 odd or even?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "odd", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "even", "ok": false, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Rules for adding", "p": [], "table": {"head": ["Sum", "Example", "Answer is…"], "rows": [["even + even", "4 + 6 = 10", "even"], ["odd + odd", "3 + 5 = 8", "even"], ["odd + even", "7 + 2 = 9", "odd"]]}, "p2": ["Why odd + odd is even: each odd number has **one left over**; the two left-overs make a **pair**."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Rules for subtracting", "p": ["Subtraction follows the same pattern: even − even = even, odd − odd = even, odd − even = odd, even − odd = odd.", "A **generalisation** is a rule that is always true. Test it with several examples – one example that fails (a **counter-example**) shows the rule is false."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Predict", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m4u03s3t02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Without adding: 357 + 128 is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "odd", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "even", "ok": false, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I use odd and even rules?", "p": ["Step 1: Look only at the ones digit of each number.", "Step 2: Decide odd or even for each.", "Step 3: Use the rule: same → even; different → odd.", "Step 4: Use it to check answers quickly."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Sum", "p": [], "q": "245 + 381?", "steps": [["odd + odd", ""]], "a": "even"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Difference", "p": [], "q": "900 − 467?", "steps": [["even − odd", ""]], "a": "odd"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Checking", "p": [], "q": "Amy says 136 + 249 = 384.", "steps": [["even + odd = odd", ""], ["384 is even", ""]], "a": "wrong (it is 385)"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Three numbers", "p": [], "q": "odd + odd + odd?", "steps": [["odd + odd = even", ""], ["even + odd = odd", ""]], "a": "odd"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Check", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m4u03s3t03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "odd − even is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "odd", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "even", "ok": false, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Thinking odd + odd is odd", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Is 15 + 9 odd or even?", "lines": ["both odd, so the answer is odd"], "bad": 0, "why": "odd + odd = even: 15 + 9 = 24.", "fix": [["even", ""]], "id": "m4u03s3t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Odd + odd = odd", "p": ["The two left-overs make a pair → even."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Teachers pairing pupils for partners and dancers in a line use odd and even thinking."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Same type (odd/odd or even/even) → even sum or difference.", "Different types → odd.", "Check with examples; one counter-example breaks a rule."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "3.3-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u03s3k01", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Before you read on: odd + odd is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "odd", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "even", "ok": true, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}}, {"id": "3.3-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u03s3k02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "odd + even is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "odd", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "even", "ok": false, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}}, {"id": "3.3-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u03s3k03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "900 − 467 is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hin